Task: 05
Title: Extension entry point (`src/index.ts`)
Phase: 1
Route: full
Slice: Foundation
Dependencies: 04
Scope: Replace the existing stub `src/index.ts` with the full extension entry point. Implement the `activate(ctx: ExtensionContext)` lifecycle hook that registers `/deepwork` and `/deepwork-resume` slash commands, registers `qrspi_dispatch` and `qrspi_question` tools, and injects the `deepwork` skill via the `resources_discover` event's `skillPaths`. The `/deepwork` command handler validates the task description, generates a run ID, creates the `.pipeline/` directory tree, creates a git branch, writes initial state, injects the orchestrator skill, and emits the kickoff message. The `/deepwork-resume` handler validates the run ID, reads `state.md`, injects the skill, and emits the resume message. Git operations skip gracefully with a warning if `git` is unavailable.
Acceptance Criteria: AC 1 (command registration), AC 2 (resume command registration), AC 5 (git-unavailable fallback)
NFRs: NFR: Reliability (resume from state), NFR: Usability (single command entry)
Gate Criteria: Phase 1 replan gate (extension activates)
Files:
  - src/index.ts (MODIFY) — Replace stub with full activate() implementation: slash command registration, tool registration, skill injection via resources_discover, /deepwork and /deepwork-resume command handlers with git branch creation and state initialization
